# pattern_gen: the pixel source `dvi_tx` and `vga_out` had no occupant
# for. Both hand out `x`, `y`, `de` and `frame` and expect a colour
# back; every design in this tree brought its own picture, so bringing
# up a board's video meant writing one before anything could be seen.
#
# Eight patterns, selected at run time so a board can put `pattern` on
# switches. Tying it to a constant folds the other seven away, which is
# why there is no parameter for which to build.
#
# It takes the active size rather than `video_timing`'s MODE on purpose:
# `ip/video/vga_out`'s README argues that the mode table should be one
# statement in one file, and a third copy of it would be a third thing
# to keep in step. `H_ACTIVE` and `V_ACTIVE` are what this block
# actually needs, and they work for a raster `video_timing` has not got.
name pattern_gen
version 1.0.0
license MIT
description "Video test patterns as a function of the raster position: colour bars, greyscale staircase, checkerboard, crosshatch, RGB steps, a solid colour, a sweeping bar and full white"

top pattern_gen
target ice40
target ecp5
target xc7

source rtl/pattern_gen.v

param H_ACTIVE int 640 1..4095
param V_ACTIVE int 480 1..4095
param SQUARE int 16 1..2048
param GRID_PITCH int 32 1..2048

port clk in
port rst_n in
port pix_en in
port de in
port frame in
port x in 12
port y in 12
port pattern in 3
port r out 8
port g out 8
port b out 8
